On Tuesday, July 16, 2013 3:36:18 PM UTC-4, Bob Carpenter wrote:<blockquote class="gmail_quote" style="margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex">n 7/16/13 2:01 PM, Ben Goodrich wrote:
<br>...
<br>&gt; 1. The case where a transformed parameter is an implicit function of data and parameters
<br>&gt;
<br>&gt; |
<br>&gt; parameters {
<br>&gt;    real alpha;
<br>&gt; }
<br>&gt; implicitly defined parameters {
<br>&gt;    real&lt;lower=l,upper=u&gt; beta;
<br>&gt;    beta &lt;- implicit( pow(beta, 5) - beta - alpha); # or something
<br>&gt; }
<br>&gt; |
<br>
<br>I take it this means beta is the solution to:
<br>
<br>    beta = beta^5 - beta - alpha.
<br></blockquote>
